  "topic_en": "A numbered list of identities between infinite products and theta-type series (1 ± 2x + 2x^4 ± ...), arranged for the theory of the arithmetic-geometric mean, using the notation [x] = (1-x)(1-x^2)(1-x^3)...",
  "transcription": "Lit. V.\n169 [-227-] 221\nDie Theoreme in Beziehung auf diejenigen Reihen und unendlichen Producte, welche zu der Theorie der arithmetisch geometrischen Mittel gehören, ordnen wir so.\n1) $(1-x)(1-xx)(1-x^3)(1-x^4)\\ldots = [x]$\n2) $(1+x)(1+xx)(1+x^3)(1+x^4)\\ldots = \\frac{[xx]}{[x]}$\n3) $(1-x)(1-x^3)(1-x^5)(1-x^7)\\ldots = \\frac{[x]}{[xx]}$\n4 $(1+x)(1+x^3)(1+x^5)(1+x^7)\\ldots = \\frac{[xx]^2}{[x]\\cdot[x^4]}$\n5 $[-x] = \\frac{[xx]^3}{[x][x^4]}$\n6 $(1+xy)(1+x^3y)(1+x^5y)\\ldots(1+xy^{-1})(1+x^3y^{-1})(1+x^5y^{-1})\\ldots$ evolvitur in seriem\n$Fx.\\{1+(y+y^{-1})x+(y^2+y^{-2})x^4+(y^3+y^{-3})x^9\\ldots]$\n7. also $Fx = \\frac{(1-x)^2(1-x^3)^2(1-x^5)^2}{1-2x+2x^4-2x^9+}$ [?] $= \\frac{[x]^2}{[xx]^2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{1-2x+2x^4-}$\n8. $Fx = \\frac{(1+xx)(1+x^6)(1+x^{10})\\ldots}{1-2x^4+2x^{16}-2x^{36}\\ldots} = \\frac{[x^4]^2}{[xx][x^8]}\\cdot\\frac{1}{1-2x^4+2x^{16}-}$\n9. $\\frac{Fx^4}{Fx} = \\frac{[xx]}{[x^8]}$ oder $[xx]Fx = [x^8]Fx^4 = [x^{32}]Fx^{16}$ [-=-] $= [x^{128}]Fx^{64}$ etc. $=1$\n10. $1-2x+2x^4-$ &c. $= \\frac{[x]^2}{[xx]} = \\frac{1-x}{1+x}\\,\\frac{1-xx}{1+xx}\\,\\frac{1-x^3}{1+x^3}$\n11. $1+2x+2x^4+$ &c. $= \\frac{[xx]^5}{[x]^2[x^4]^2} = \\frac{1+x}{1-x}\\,\\frac{1-xx}{1+xx}\\,\\frac{1+x^3}{1-x^3}\\,\\frac{1-x^4}{1+x^4}$ [?]\nAndere Beweise dieser Sätze\nWenn man in 6 statt y, xy schreibt so wird\n$(1+\\frac{1}{yy})(1+xxyy)(1+x^4yy)(1+x^6yy)\\ldots(1+xxy^{-2})(1+x^4y^{-2})\\ldots = \\frac{1}{[xx]}\\{(1+y^{-2})+(y^2+y^{-4})xx+(y^4+y^{-6})x^6+\\&c.\\}$\noder\n12. $(y+\\frac{1}{y})(1+xxyy)(1+x^4yy)(1+x^6yy)\\ldots(1+xxy^{-2})(1+x^4y^{-2})\\ldots = \\frac{1}{[xx]x^{\\frac14}}\\{(y+y^{-1})x^{\\frac14}+(y^3+y^{-3})x^{\\frac94}+$ &c.$\\}$\nAndere Beweis\n13 $x^{\\frac14}\\frac{[x^4]^2}{[xx]} = x^{\\frac14}+x^{\\frac94}+$ &c. oder\n14. $\\frac{[xx]^2}{[x]} = 1+x+x^3+x^6+x^{10}\\ldots = \\frac{1-xx}{1-x}\\,\\frac{1-x^4}{1-x^3}$\nAndere Beweise\n15. $(1-2x+2x^4-)(1+2x+2x^4) = (1-2xx+2x^8)^2$\n16 $(1-2x+2x^4)^2+(1+2x+2x^4)^2 = 2(1+2xx+2x^8)^2$\n17 $(1+2x+2x^4)(x^{\\frac14}+x^{\\frac94}\\ldots) = (x^{\\frac18}+x^{\\frac98}\\ldots)^2$\n18 $(1+2x+2x^4)^2+(2x^{\\frac14}+2x^{\\frac94}\\ldots)^2 = (1+2x^{\\frac12}+2x^2+)^2$",
